by campaign and show unusually large undecided blocs, so they justify only a modest shift toward competitiveness from the fundamentals.", "watch": "An independent October poll confirming a single-digit race, or a late surge in Crosby's fundraising or outside spending, would move this toward a genuine contest.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Blake Moore (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Blake Moore, the Republican incumbent, is seeking another term in a northern Utah district that has leaned about 15 points Republican in recent elections. He faces Democrat Peter Crosby, along with independent and Libertarian candidates on the ballot. Moore has raised roughly $2.5 million to Crosby's $138,000, and outside spending has been modest and roughly balanced. Prediction markets give Crosby about a 4 to 5 percent chance of winning.\n\nPolling is sparse. The only independent survey, from late September, had Moore ahead by five among likely voters, while two polls sponsored by the Crosby campaign showed a one-to-three-point race with more than a quarter of respondents undecided. The district's fundamentals, the fundraising gap, and market pricing all point to a Republican hold, with the close-looking surveys treated cautiously given their sponsorship and high undecided shares.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0822, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0948, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0534, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.112, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2129, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1726, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1389, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_de